  "_toolbox": {
    "status": "tested",
    "testedOn": "UPS widgets: a production Polaris install (exported 2026-10-23); PDU widgets: built from PowerNet-MIB, not yet tested",
    "date": "2026-10-23",
    "note": "One APC profile governs every APC product, so every widget is scoped by modelPattern. UPS widgets (w1-w8, PowerNet-MIB ups*) carry 'UPS|Symmetra|Galaxy' — UPS models come from this profile's upsBasicIdentModel row. Rack PDU widgets (w9-w17, PowerNet-MIB rPDU2*) carry '^(AP8|APDU)' — a 2G/3G rack PDU's model comes from its management card's sysDescr (MN:AP8870, Polaris rule 161). PDU Power uses hundredths_to_units, which needs Polaris with that transform (added 2026-11-11); an older install imports it with no transform, so it reads 100 times too high — update Polaris first. Added 2026-11-11, not yet tested on a PDU: Outlet Power's unit is unstated in the MIB (watts by common use; compare with the PDU's web page), Outlet State and Outlet Power read only on switched / metered-by-outlet models, and Bank Load State only on banked models. Probe Temperature (rPDU2SensorTempHumidityStatusTempC) was removed 2026-11-11 after its first run: with no probe attached the PDU still answers the row with -1 (TempStatus notPresent), which a gauge cannot tell from a reading and shows as -0.1 C; add it by hand, switched on only for PDUs with a probe fitted."
  }
}
